946	     * {@code normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)} (see
947	     * {@link #identityKey(Owner)}) and is the single duplicate check: it subsumes the former separate
948	     * telephone, email and household duplicate blocks. Because the telephone is part of the key, two
949	     * owners with the same last name and postcode but <em>different</em> telephones have different
950	     * identity keys and are both allowed (the second is surfaced instead as a soft
951	     * {@code possibleDuplicate}, see {@link #possibleDuplicateOf(Owner)}); only an exact full-key match
952	     * is a duplicate. Owners flagged deleted are ignored (see {@link #findExistingOwner(Function, String)}),
953	     * and the email-domain blocklist has already been applied earlier in the create flow. A collision is
954	     * reported through a {@link DuplicateOwnerIdentityException}, which the {@code ExceptionControllerAdvice}
